    <marc:datafield tag="520" ind1=" " ind2=" ">
      <marc:subfield code="a">Synopsis: This course contains materials for Form 3 Science on the topic Reproduction of Flowering Plants and Pollination. It aims to help students the topic better. It emphasizes on observatory skill and the study of the structures of a flower, meaning of pollination, types of pollination and pollination agents. Creative and critical thinking skill are encouraged through the exercises and suggested activities. At the end of the lesson, pupils can be tested with the evaluations questions provided.</marc:subfield>
